\section{The ordering contract}{

\code{\link[=grin_infer]{grin_infer()}} trusts \code{counts} to already be canonical. A wrong guess about
stimulus/response order returns a confident wrong posterior, so it is never
guessed: \code{\link[=grin_to_confusion]{grin_to_confusion()}} either resolves the order from labels you supply,
or requires you to assert \code{order = "canonical"}.
